232
00:10:14,172 --> 00:10:15,924
Yo, Dee!

233
00:10:20,053 --> 00:10:22,722
- I don't know what you're doing.
- Do what Coach is saying.

234
00:10:23,473 --> 00:10:26,433
I don't know what any of this shit means.
How about I just throw the goddamn ball?

235
00:10:26,434 --> 00:10:28,228
- Okay?
- Whoo, you got this!

236
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:33,524
Strike one!

237
00:10:33,525 --> 00:10:35,109
- This is gonna be good.
- It is, yeah.

238
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:36,694
This is gonna be good.

239
00:10:39,114 --> 00:10:41,700
- Strike two!
- Here we go!

240
00:10:42,450 --> 00:10:44,493
Strike three!

241
00:10:47,372 --> 00:10:49,957
- Strike three!
- Oh, come on!

242
00:10:53,128 --> 00:10:56,214
- Strike three!
- It's so easy!

243
00:10:56,715 --> 00:10:57,965
It's just too easy!

244
00:11:03,138 --> 00:11:05,889
You got nothing!

245
00:11:08,143 --> 00:11:09,309
Strike two!

246
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:11,145
You suck!

247
00:11:11,146 --> 00:11:13,231
You're a loser! You're a loser!

248
00:11:15,191 --> 00:11:17,693
We have ourselves
a heck of a pitching duel

249
00:11:17,694 --> 00:11:20,362
as the bats on both teams
have gone ice-cold.

250
00:11:20,363 --> 00:11:22,490
Have to admire the stamina
of the 50-year-old.

251
00:11:23,908 --> 00:11:27,077
Strike three!

252
00:11:27,078 --> 00:11:30,205
As we can tell, she's in agony
with each remaining pitch.

253
00:11:30,206 --> 00:11:31,623
Way to go, Dee!

254
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:33,208
- Way to go!
- Oh, God.

255
00:11:33,209 --> 00:11:35,544
My goddamn arm, it's about to break off.

256
00:11:35,545 --> 00:11:37,963
Get her some ice, Mac!
Dee, your work's almost done.

257
00:11:37,964 --> 00:11:40,340
One more run, boys, we win this thing!

258
00:11:40,341 --> 00:11:43,302
- You got your cup in, Dee?
- Get off me! Jesus.

259
00:11:43,303 --> 00:11:45,429
Nothing, nothing in the final inning

260
00:11:45,430 --> 00:11:49,349
as Paddy's has managed
to load the bases with two outs.

261
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:52,436
- Lucky, you're up!
- What?

262
00:11:52,437 --> 00:11:56,107
Lucky, I'm putting you in the game.

263
00:11:57,358 --> 00:12:00,194
I want you to lay down the
suicide squeeze.

264
00:12:00,195 --> 00:12:01,362
{\an8}What's he saying?

265
00:12:01,863 --> 00:12:04,490
- He's saying he wants you to bunt.
- I want you to bunt.

266
00:12:04,491 --> 00:12:06,909
- Just put on the helmet.
- Yeah, get out there, Lucky!

267
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:08,119
- There you go.
- You got this.

268
00:12:08,703 --> 00:12:09,996
Batter up!

269
00:12:14,042 --> 00:12:15,210
Who's this kid?

270
00:12:16,878 --> 00:12:19,254
- What are you listening to?
- You talking to me?

271
00:12:19,255 --> 00:12:22,674
- Yes, what are you listening to?
- I'm listening to the kid in the booth.

272
00:12:22,675 --> 00:12:24,843
He's incredible.
He's like a modern-day Vin Scully.

273
00:12:24,844 --> 00:12:28,388
Well, knock it off and get your head
back in the game. Who is this kid?

274
00:12:28,389 --> 00:12:30,224
I-I don't know, Frank.
There's no stats on him.

275
00:12:30,225 --> 00:12:32,851
- He's never actually made it to bat.
- Fuck me.

276
00:12:32,852 --> 00:12:35,313
Hey, death squad, do something.

277
00:12:51,579 --> 00:12:53,789
Time! Dead ball, take your base.

278
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:55,791
Ah! He got hit in the balls!

279
00:12:55,792 --> 00:12:58,627
- We win, we win, we win! He gets on base.
- Oh, we win.

280
00:12:58,628 --> 00:12:59,879
Ball game!

281
00:13:00,755 --> 00:13:01,798
We won!

282
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:07,928
- Hey, Coach. That's why you wear a cup.
- Uh-oh.

283
00:13:07,929 --> 00:13:10,014
- Oh, shit.
- Uh-oh.

284
00:13:17,939 --> 00:13:22,101
No. What happened out there
was unacceptable.

285
00:13:22,694 --> 00:13:24,319
What are you talking about, Frank? We won.

286
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,072
We won
because of a hit by pitch. You got lucky.

287
00:13:27,073 --> 00:13:29,783
Damn right we got lucky.
That's because of our lucky little fella.

288
00:13:29,784 --> 00:13:34,538
See, Charlie knows that it's baseball luck
to have a special needs kid on the team.

289
00:13:34,539 --> 00:13:36,456
- What do your stats say about that?
- Yeah.

290
00:13:36,457 --> 00:13:38,792
The problem is, of course,
he's now out for the season,

291
00:13:38,793 --> 00:13:42,045
and we're gonna need
a new special needs kid.

292
00:13:42,046 --> 00:13:45,674
- Possibly a tad more severe case. Yeah.
- You wanna up the case.

293
00:13:45,675 --> 00:13:48,051
- No Albanians!
- No, no, can't have Albanians.

294
00:13:48,052 --> 00:13:51,054
You know what? I don't have my book on me,
but I know the stats don't support that,

295
00:13:51,055 --> 00:13:53,307
and you are all turned around
on this Albanian thing.

296
00:13:53,308 --> 00:13:58,478
Yeah, look, I spent top dollar
on this team, and I want results.

297
00:13:58,479 --> 00:13:59,813
Why's Frank get a hot dog?

298
00:13:59,814 --> 00:14:02,024
You guys both have hot dogs?
I want a hot dog.

299
00:14:02,025 --> 00:14:03,108
The spoils.

300
00:14:03,109 --> 00:14:05,277
- Buy the team, you get the hot dogs.
- Mmm.

301
00:14:05,278 --> 00:14:07,487
- Hot dog.
- Who's pitching today?

302
00:14:07,488 --> 00:14:09,364
- It's got to be Jones.
- Yes, I think it's got to be Jones

303
00:14:09,365 --> 00:14:11,283
because he's got
a pretty good splitter, so...

304
00:14:11,284 --> 00:14:13,035
- Wrong.
- It's Dee again.

305
00:14:13,036 --> 00:14:14,870
- Dee.
- Dee? No, her arm is shot.

306
00:14:14,871 --> 00:14:17,706
Can't afford to lose this game, Coach.
Gotta do whatever it takes.

307
00:14:17,707 --> 00:14:20,751
- Stats support it.
- You talking about, "All about the stats."

308
00:14:23,546 --> 00:14:25,547
But you're not taking my baseball!

309
00:14:25,548 --> 00:14:28,216
Ah! You know what this is?
That's my baseball!

310
00:14:28,217 --> 00:14:29,384
It's all my baseballs.

311
00:14:32,013 --> 00:14:33,555
What'd he say?

312
00:14:33,556 --> 00:14:37,392
Yeah, he didn't drink any water and we
won the game, and he's so superstitious.

313
00:14:37,393 --> 00:14:40,313
I have not seen him take any fluids
for 48 hours.

314
00:14:42,774 --> 00:14:44,733
I should probably go check on him.

315
00:14:44,734 --> 00:14:46,360
Hey, Coach! Coach?

316
00:14:48,112 --> 00:14:49,113
Who you calling?

317
00:14:49,614 --> 00:14:52,532
I gotta make some changes.
I need to get some more ringers.

318
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:54,327
Also, you're fired.

319
00:14:55,161 --> 00:14:56,454
I'm fired? Why am I fired?

320
00:14:57,372 --> 00:15:00,666
You listen to the play-by-play,
eating all my dogs,

321
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:02,334
and it's not working out.

322
00:15:02,335 --> 00:15:04,253
We're just gonna go
in a different direction.

323
00:15:05,213 --> 00:15:07,506
<i>- Hola.
- Hola. Mmm.</i>

324
00:15:07,507 --> 00:15:11,593
All right, boys, let's go, stretch it out.
We got a beautiful day for baseball.

325
00:15:11,594 --> 00:15:12,595
Hey, hey.

326
00:15:13,096 --> 00:15:14,888
What's going on over here?

327
00:15:14,889 --> 00:15:16,640
Hey, Coach Bob.
You got a new coaching gig?

328
00:15:16,641 --> 00:15:19,393
- Who the heck are all these kids?
- Oh, these guys.

329
00:15:19,394 --> 00:15:24,731
Yeah, this is, uh, Philepe, Jose,
Ramiriz, Cortez, Ramon...

330
00:15:28,319 --> 00:15:30,529
What's with the crazy person
in the corner?

331
00:15:31,698 --> 00:15:33,407
Ah, we picked up a new lucky little fella.

332
00:15:33,408 --> 00:15:35,575
He's not little.

333
00:15:35,576 --> 00:15:38,495
Best we can do on short notice, Dee.
We tied him down to be safe.

334
00:15:38,496 --> 00:15:40,372
- I think that's for the best, yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

335
00:15:40,373 --> 00:15:43,166
- Just don't go near him.
- I wasn't planning on it.

336
00:15:43,167 --> 00:15:46,044
Don't listen to the girl, Lucky.
Look at the game, look at the game.

337
00:15:46,045 --> 00:15:48,213
Hey, Lucky.

338
00:15:48,214 --> 00:15:52,926
Breathe, breathe, Lucky, all right? Stay!

339
00:15:52,927 --> 00:15:55,929
Well, Timmy, looks like we are in
for a good one today

340
00:15:55,930 --> 00:15:59,891
as the Paddy's Pinstripes have replaced
their entire starting lineup

341
00:15:59,892 --> 00:16:02,519
with what appears to be
international talent.

342
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,730
An unorthodox move.

343
00:16:04,731 --> 00:16:08,567
Almost as unorthodox as Dennis Reynolds,
a man I've never met,

344
00:16:08,568 --> 00:16:10,736
joining me in the booth today, folks.

345
00:16:10,737 --> 00:16:15,407
That's right, Tim,
and with approximately 84,000 children

346
00:16:15,408 --> 00:16:18,201
abducted each year,
you do wanna be careful.

347
00:16:18,202 --> 00:16:23,165
That said, uh, 93% of those children
do turn out to be runaways,

348
00:16:23,166 --> 00:16:25,375
so the numbers are in your favor.

349
00:16:25,376 --> 00:16:28,253
It's a strange and disturbing factoid,
Dennis.

350
00:16:28,254 --> 00:16:30,881
<i>Seventy-two degrees
on this beautiful afternoon</i>

351
00:16:30,882 --> 00:16:32,924
<i>as the Pinstripes take the field.</i>

352
00:16:32,925 --> 00:16:37,095
<i>Let's hope for a good game today
as Deandra Reynolds takes the mound</i>

353
00:16:37,096 --> 00:16:39,181
<i>for a second game in a row.</i>

354
00:16:40,349 --> 00:16:42,976
A chorus of boos for Reynolds.

355
00:16:44,771 --> 00:16:46,522
Oh, fuck you! Charlie!

356
00:16:48,649 --> 00:16:51,401
Charlie, my arm's about to die.
I think I only got one inning in me.

357
00:16:51,402 --> 00:16:53,613
- You think you got one?
- I think I only got one.

358
00:16:55,031 --> 00:16:56,032
Oh, God.

359
00:17:03,956 --> 00:17:04,957
Yeah, what?

360
00:17:05,875 --> 00:17:08,794
No, no, no, no, no. She's staying in.
She's staying in!

361
00:17:14,383 --> 00:17:16,844
- You're going the distance.
- What--

362
00:17:18,429 --> 00:17:20,056
Drink a goddamn glass of water!

363
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:24,685
Strike!

364
00:17:25,770 --> 00:17:26,854
Keep your eyes open.

365
00:17:27,396 --> 00:17:28,397
Stupid kid.

366
00:17:29,565 --> 00:17:31,609
- Strike, you're out!
- Come on!

367
00:17:32,610 --> 00:17:34,194
Oh, it's gone!

368
00:17:37,698 --> 00:17:40,617
Strike! Strike! Strike!

369
00:17:40,618 --> 00:17:43,036
Yeah, yeah, you suck.

370
00:17:48,209 --> 00:17:49,210
Nice.

371
00:17:51,295 --> 00:17:53,505
- Strike three!
- Go, you're gone. You're good.

372
00:17:53,506 --> 00:17:55,549
It's third strike, dum-dum.

373
00:17:55,550 --> 00:17:56,843
Come on!

374
00:17:58,845 --> 00:18:02,097
Oh, oh, oh. Out of there!

375
00:18:02,098 --> 00:18:05,308
Pinstripes looking absolutely dominant
out there today.

376
00:18:05,309 --> 00:18:08,270
They are,
but Reynolds showing signs of fatigue.

377
00:18:08,271 --> 00:18:11,523
You have to wonder how long
that 50-year-old arm can keep this up

378
00:18:11,524 --> 00:18:13,984
as the Pinstripe's manager comes out
to the mound.

379
00:18:13,985 --> 00:18:15,944
Please, God, take me out. You have to.

380
00:18:15,945 --> 00:18:17,320
The thing about you is

381
00:18:17,321 --> 00:18:18,531
you're a natural.

382
00:18:19,449 --> 00:18:20,647
You got one more batter.

383
00:18:20,647 --> 00:18:24,203
I gotta trust my gut.

384
00:18:25,288 --> 00:18:28,582
The only word I understood was "gut,"
and yours is flooded with seed oils.

385
00:18:28,583 --> 00:18:30,125
All right, you've got this, man.

386
00:18:30,126 --> 00:18:32,128
- You've got this, man.
- Okay, stop it!

387
00:18:32,879 --> 00:18:36,256
This is the last batter, though!
This is the last one!

388
00:18:58,029 --> 00:18:59,404
- What's this?
- That's not good.

389
00:18:59,405 --> 00:19:00,739
No!

390
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:04,659
- I heard it all the way in here, Talhoon.
- So did I, Dennis.

391
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,077
Yeah, I'll bet.

392
00:19:06,078 --> 00:19:12,000
Uh, fun fact, elongated noodle arms
are 57% more prone to dislocate

393
00:19:12,001 --> 00:19:16,546
and 92% when their owner has
weak ligaments and shit posture,

394
00:19:16,547 --> 00:19:19,382
not to mention the sheer amount
of alcohol abuse.

395
00:19:19,383 --> 00:19:22,427
And she's a bitch and a bird.
Back to you, Tim.

396
00:19:22,428 --> 00:19:25,096
Oh, God.

397
00:19:25,097 --> 00:19:26,098
Suck it up!

398
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:29,226
Probably should've pulled her earlier.

399
00:19:29,227 --> 00:19:30,310
- Yeah, I think so.
- Yeah.

400
00:19:30,311 --> 00:19:31,686
Hold on, what's this now?

401
00:19:36,859 --> 00:19:39,152
And in comes ICE.

402
00:19:39,153 --> 00:19:41,738
<i>Oh. Very regrettable scene here, Timmy,</i>

403
00:19:41,739 --> 00:19:44,574
<i>as ICE agents scramble
to detain the children.</i>

404
00:19:44,575 --> 00:19:46,368
Oh, God, no!

405
00:19:46,369 --> 00:19:47,670
Don't let him get you!

406
00:19:47,954 --> 00:19:51,289
Have to wonder if that call came
from Pinstripe former coach, Bob D'Marco,

407
00:19:51,290 --> 00:19:53,583
as the new Pinstripe brass is
in a tailspin.

408
00:19:53,584 --> 00:19:55,627
Oh, shit.

409
00:19:55,628 --> 00:19:56,711
Do something.

410
00:20:01,425 --> 00:20:03,510
And here comes the lucky fella,

411
00:20:03,511 --> 00:20:07,430
Pinstripes' mongoloid mascot
loose on the field.

412
00:20:07,431 --> 00:20:09,516
It's pandemonium, Dennis.

413
00:20:09,517 --> 00:20:11,810
Not sure "mongoloid"
is the appropriate term.

414
00:20:11,811 --> 00:20:15,146
Oh, it is, Timmy. It is.
It's derived from the word "Mongolian."

415
00:20:15,147 --> 00:20:18,858
But in a surprising twist,
the man is actually Albanian.

416
00:20:18,859 --> 00:20:21,236
- Mmm.
- I don't know the playbook for this one.

417
00:20:21,237 --> 00:20:23,822
Nope. It looks like
it's gonna sort itself out.

418
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:25,282
- Yeah.
- Let's get you some water.

419
00:20:25,283 --> 00:20:27,576
Oh, that would be good. Let's go.
Let's get some water.

420
00:20:28,661 --> 00:20:32,290
You hate to see it, Timmy.
It's a dark day for baseball.

421
00:20:32,915 --> 00:20:34,165
Sure is.

